---
description: Backend conventions for NestJS and Prisma
globs:
  - "backend/**"
alwaysApply: false
---
- Use a modular NestJS 12 monolith under `backend/`; controllers stay thin and business rules live in services. Compile with TypeScript 6. Do not install TypeScript 7 for the Nest CLI.
- Validate every external DTO; use explicit authorization and ownership checks per resource.
- PostgreSQL constraints and transactions enforce invariants; do not rely on frontend checks.
- Collection + score updates must be atomic and idempotent; add unique constraints for replay protection.
- Add indexes for demonstrated query patterns, not speculatively.
- Use migrations; never edit production data/schema manually.
- Keep REST APIs documented and errors predictable. Avoid premature queues, caches, and microservices.
